libheif and libde265 (LGPL-3.0)
-------------------------------

Image conversion for HEIC/HEIF inputs uses libheif 1.23.2 (LGPL-3.0-or-later),
built with libde265 1.0.15 (LGPL-3.0-or-later) as its HEVC decoder. Both are
used UNMODIFIED, through the `libheif-js` package, and neither is statically
linked into any binary of ours: this product runs from TypeScript source and
loads libheif at runtime from files on disk.

  - Upstream: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif and
    https://github.com/strukturag/libde265
  - Distribution used: https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js
  - License texts, as shipped: node_modules/libheif-js/LICENSE (LGPL-3.0) and
    node_modules/libheif-js/libheif/LICENSE (LGPL-3.0, GPL-3.0 and MIT)

REPLACING THE LIBRARY. You may replace libheif with any interface-compatible
build, and nothing of ours needs rebuilding to do it:

  - the WebAssembly binary is a single file, node_modules/libheif-js/
    libheif-wasm/libheif.wasm, and the path it is loaded from is overridable at
    runtime with the VISION_LIBHEIF_WASM_PATH environment variable; or
  - replace the node_modules/libheif-js directory with your own build of the
    package.

The bundled variant of that package (libheif-js/wasm-bundle) is deliberately NOT
what this product loads, for exactly this reason: it carries the same binary
base64-encoded inside a 1.9 MB JavaScript file, which nothing can replace
without rebuilding the package.

